    {
      "check_id": "typed-relation-edge-non-collapse",
      "detail": "Artifact instance identity, Ontology Node identity, and the represented subject binding are three separate values. Typed Relation identity and Ontology Edge identity remain separate even for a projected edge. One global Typed Relation may be projected into several Ontologies; each edge has its own ontology-local lifecycle. Retiring a projected Ontology Edge does not retire its global Typed Relation; retiring a global Typed Relation does not erase historical ontology events. An ontology-local edge never becomes global through export, projection, schema validity, shared labels, or repeated use. Ontology lifecycle active, retired, removed remains independent of admission, maturity, promotion, confidence, projection freshness, and runtime activation. Semantic events change meaning-bearing state; governance events record governance posture for an exact semantic epoch and cannot rewrite it. A calculated Cut, View, snapshot, index, graph, or Markdown rendering is never accepted as canonical replay input.",
